    pr_ref:  # 7a46
    description: "Found by the 2026-10-20 docstring-staleness audit (verifier reproduced). `_extract_scheme_edges` treats every non-special-form list as a call, including the children of a let/let*/letrec binding list, so `(define (g) (let ((z 1)) (helper z)))` yields g -> scheme:unresolved:z beside g -> helper. Racket has the same defect for parenthesised bindings; square-bracket bindings `[z 1]` are not affected. Fix: skip the binding list of let-family forms (walk only each binding's init expression)."  # 7a46
    fields: {}  # 7a46
